      "problem": "Which statement is equivalent to $(A∧C)∨(B∧A)?$",
      "worked_solution": "First,  since $A∨C≡C∨A,$ we can write\n\n$$\n(A∧C)∨(B∧A)≡(C∧A)∨(B∧A).\n$$\n\nThen,  we can factor out the conjunction with $A,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n(C∧A)∨(B∧A)≡(C∨B)∧A\n$$",
